  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 326 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nDry weather is expected to continue through Thursday the LREF is \nshowing a upper high building over the southern Plains.  The LREF is \nstill showing a trough dropping southeast across the Midwest late in \nthe week with a 40-60% chance of showers and thunderstorms on \nFriday.   This is at the same time when the ECWMF/GFS is showing \nhigh PWATS coupled with a strong LLJ and WPC is highlighting central \nMO with a slight risk for excessive rainfall, so we will need \nto keep an eye out for locally heavy rainfall. Otherwise, the \nLREF is showing a ridge building over the central CONUS with the\nNBM keeping the upcoming weekend dry. \n\nThe relief from the warm weather is expected to continue through \nlate week with high temperatures 5-10 degrees below normal through \nFriday.  Highs will rise back above normal over the weekend as 850mb \ntemperatures climb back above +20C.",
